721,2024-06-04 00:00:00,2024,Reported Use of Purportedly AI-Generated Student Accounts in Online College Courses,"An adjunct professor at an unspecified community college reportedly suspected that some students in his online art history and art appreciation courses are AI-powered spambots. These ""students"" allegedly submitted peculiar assignments, such as analyses of non-existent artworks and descriptions of sculptures using painting terminology. Additionally, their engagement with the college portal is reportedly minimal. The professor reportedly believed the spambot students aimed to fraudulently obtain financial aid by remaining enrolled in courses.","Financial Aid Scammers, Scammers","Unknown Spambot Creators, Generative Ai Developers","Students, Professors, General Public, Epistemic Integrity, Community Colleges, Academic Staff, Educational Communities, University Students",642188372947D07020C1319D,Unknown Generative Ai Systems,2026-05-18 01:27:13,"Please also refer to Incident 1038: Scammers Reportedly Use AI Tools to Impersonate Students and Obtain Federal Aid. While no specific link has been established, the incidents appear to reflect similar patterns of AI-assisted enrollment fraud. They are treated as distinct due to lack of direct evidence connecting them.",MIT,1,Malicious Actors & Misuse,"Fraud, scams, and targeted manipulation",AI,Intentional,Post-deployment,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,1,Intentional human misuse
