877,2024-12-16 00:00:00,2024,HTML/Nomani Deepfake Phishing Campaigns Allegedly Use AI-Generated Content to Defraud Social Media Users,"AI-generated deepfakes were reportedly used in the ""HTML/Nomani"" phishing campaign to mimic legitimate platforms like booking services and lured victims into investment scams. These scams allegedly leveraged realistic fake content to deceive users on social media for the purposes of financial fraud. This campaign was part of the rising misuse of AI in cybercrime during the second half of 2024.","Htmlnomani, Scammers",Deepfake Technology Developers,"Phishing Victims, Booking.Com Customers, Booking.Com, Airbnb Users, Airbnb",642188372947D07020C1319D,"Ai Powered Cryptostealers, Ai Enhanced Ransomware Systems, Deepfake Technology",2024-12-18 13:11:10,"For more information, see the full ESET threat report, including how Lumma Stealer malware reportedly surged in targeting macOS and mobile users, and how RansomHub ransomware allegedly employed AI-driven techniques to enhance evasion and effectiveness, at the following URL: https://web-assets.esetstatic.com/wls/en/papers/threat-reports/eset-threat-report-h22024.pdf. See also: Incident 870: Meeten Malware Campaign Reportedly Undermines Web3 Security Using AI-Legitimized Branding.",MIT,1,Malicious Actors & Misuse,"Fraud, scams, and targeted manipulation",Human,Intentional,Post-deployment,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,1,Intentional human misuse
